.TH TDU_WEBSERVER 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tdu_webserver \- TDU embedded web server with a bulk spill-history route
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python2.5
.B contrib/tduweb/tdu_webserver.py
.RI [ PORT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tdu_webserver.py
is a drop-in replacement for
.I TDUWeb/server/tdu_webserver.py
on a NOvA Timing Distribution Unit. It is a small
.B bottle
application that runs the TDU's command-line utilities and returns their
output over HTTP. Every existing route issues the same command as before, and
one route is added,
.IR /spill_history ,
which is what
.BR darpa-spill-server (1)
needs to record a complete event history.
.PP
The copy in this repository is a mirror. The authoritative, deployed file is
.I server/tdu_webserver.py
on the
.B Darpa\-Modifications
branch of
.BR https://github.com/NovaDAQ/TDUWeb .
Change it there, then re-sync.
.PP
It runs on the TDU's stock Python 2.5 as well as Python 3, needs nothing
beyond the vendored
.I bottle.py
already in
.IR TDUWeb/server/ ,
and carries its own JSON encoder because Python 2.5 has no
.B json
module. It works with an unpatched
.B DumpSpillHistory
by parsing that tool's CSV output.
.PP
bottle's default server is single-threaded, so every helper command is run
with a 20 s timeout, and its output is capped at 8 MiB, so that one hung or
oversized command cannot take down every route.
.SH ROUTES
.TP
.B /tcr_status
.TQ
.B /onehz_status
The newest event in the
.B BEAM
shared-memory ring, from
.BR "DumpSpillHistory \-\-last" .
Both return the same record, because
.B \-\-last
ignores the type filters.
.TP
.BR /spill_history "[?since=\fITICKS\fR&until=\fITICKS\fR&limit=\fIN\fR&types=\fILIST\fR]"
A window of events as JSON:
.BR since " (inclusive) and " until
(exclusive) in NOvA ticks, decimal or
.BR 0x \-hex;
.B limit
default 5000, capped at 20000;
.B types
a comma-separated list of decoded spill-type numbers. The body is
.B {"events": [...], "count": N, "truncated": B, "limit": L}
with rows oldest first. When
.B truncated
is true, ask again with
.B since
past the last row.
.TP
.B /spill_history_info
Capabilities, for client probing: limits, the memory segment, and whether the
raw event word is available (it is not).
.TP
.B /tdu_status
.BR tduRegDump .
.TP
.BR /tdu_init ", " /tdu_sync
.BR "tduControl set 0x0 0x0420" .
.TP
.B /tdu_scrub
.BR "tduControl set 0x0009 0x0004" .
.TP
.BR /tdu_errors ", " /tdu_errors2
.B tduRegDump \-w \-a
.BR 0x0014 " and " 0x000e .
.TP
.B /tcr_start
Launches
.B "TCRMonitor \-D 0 \-S 0"
and returns at once. The original blocked forever waiting for a process that
never exits; this is the one intentional change in behaviour.
.TP
.B /tcr_running
Whether a
.B TCRMonitor
process exists
.RB ( pidof ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PORT
Port to listen on. Wins over
.BR TDU_WEB_PORT .
A value that is not a number in 1\(en65535 is reported on standard error and
ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TDU_WEB_HOST
Address to bind. Default \fB0.0.0.0\fR.
.TP
.B TDU_WEB_PORT
Port to bind when no
.I PORT
argument is given. Default \fB8080\fR.
.TP
.B TDU_WEB_NO_SERVE
Set to \fB1\fR, \fBtrue\fR or \fByes\fR to import the module without starting
the server, as
.BR tduweb-selftest (1)
and linters do. Without it, importing the module starts the server, as the
original did.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install on the TDU, as root, keeping the original for rollback:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cd /path/to/TDUWeb/server
cp tdu_webserver.py tdu_webserver.py.orig\-$(date +%Y%m%d)
cp /path/from/here/tdu_webserver.py tdu_webserver.py
.EE
.RE
.PP
Restart the service, then check the new route and an old one:
.PP
.RS
.EX
curl \-s 'http://localhost:8080/spill_history?limit=5' | head
curl \-s 'http://localhost:8080/tcr_status'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run on another port:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python2.5 ./tdu_webserver.py 8081
TDU_WEB_PORT=8081 python2.5 ./tdu_webserver.py
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I contrib/tduweb/README.md
Why the route is needed, deployment, rollback, and the further upstream
changes it does not make.
.TP
.I contrib/tduweb/patches/0001\-DumpSpillHistory\-json\-and\-time\-window.patch
Optional fix to
.BR DumpSpillHistory 's
bulk JSON, adding
.BR \-\-since / \-\-until .
